><link rel="profile" href="http://gmpg.org/xfn/11"/><link rel="pingback" href="https://www.geeksforgeeks.org/x lrpc.php"/><script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"VideoObject","name":"Linux  Command Usage","description":"Linux is a Unix-Like operating system. All the LinuxUnix commands are run in the terminal provided by the Linux system. This terminal is just like the command prompt of Windows OS. LinuxUnix commands are case-sensitive. The terminal can be used to accomplish all Administrative tasks. This includes package installation, file manipulation, and user management. Linux terminal is user-interactive. The terminal outputs the results of commands which are specified by the user itself. Execution of typed command is done only after you press the Enter key.Command Usagehttpswww.geeksforgeeks.orglinux-commands","thumbnailUrl":["https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/geeksforgeeks/LinuxCommandUsage/LinuxCommandUsage20221213174956.jpg","https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/geeksforgeeks/LinuxCommandUsage/LinuxCommandUsage20221213174956-seo.png","https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/geeksforgeeks/LinuxCommandUsage/LinuxCommandUsage20221213174956-small.png"],"uploadDate":"2022-05-11T11:24:54Z","duration":"PT0H8M2S","contentUrl":"https://www.geeksforgeeks.org/videos/linux-command-usage/"}</script><script>
